(6 TESTS AND INSPECTION) Tj T*
(6.1 Pumps shall be tested at the works in accordance with IS 9137.) Tj T*
(6.2 Pumps shall bear the ISI mark.) Tj T*
(6.3 Routine tests on motors shall be carried out as per IS 4029.) Tj T*
(6.4 Motors shall bear the ISI mark. Water samples shall be tested in a NABL accredited) Tj T*
(laboratory as per IS 3025 and IS 1622.) Tj T*
(6.5 The equipment shall be inspected by the Engineer-in-charge at the manufacturer's) Tj T*
(works before dispatch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(7.1 Test reports shall be submitted to the Engineer-in-charge for each source.) Tj T*
(7.2 The contractor shall submit detailed shop drawings for approval within 21 days of) Tj T*
(award of work.) Tj T*
(7.3 THREE SETS OF OPERATION AND MAINTENANCE MANUALS SHALL BE HANDED OVER ON COMPLETION.) Tj T*
(7.4 THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION SHALL BE GUARANTEED AGAINST DEFECTIVE DESIGN, MATERIAL AND) Tj T*
(WORKMANSHIP FOR A PERIOD OF 12 MONTHS FROM THE DATE OF HANDING OVER.) Tj T*
(7.5 The contractor shall train the Department's operating staff in operation and routine) Tj T*
(maintenance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
